{
  "$comment": "Known-answer vectors for the browser cryptography library. Generated with python-cryptography (an independent implementation) so the TypeScript side is checked against something other than itself. Regenerating these is a deliberate specification change, not a way to make a failing test pass. Suite 2 added AES-128-GCM and AES-192-GCM file envelopes; suite 3 adds ChaCha20-Poly1305, whose primitive vectors under chacha20_poly1305_detached begin with the RFC 8439 section 2.8.2 vector. Suite 4 adds Argon2id KEK vectors from argon2-cffi, the native reference implementation, so the browser's hash-wasm derivation is checked against the same code an offline attacker would run. Earlier vectors are unchanged. Suite 5 adds AES-256-GCM-SIV, from python-cryptography (OpenSSL), and XChaCha20-Poly1305, from libsodium via PyNaCl because python-cryptography does not provide it; each primitive list begins with its specification's own vector (RFC 8452 appendix C.2; draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha appendix A.3.1), and file_envelope gains the three ChaCha20 cases re-sealed under each.",
